			y: 6.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"415F2703877FBE21"
				"36DF9A3674E1212C"
			]
			description: [
				"With your &3Prismatic Crucible&r, you are now able to process &6Prismatic Cores&r. Starting as Inert, run the Core through each consecutive primary/secondary color to progress the core. Once you've reached Magenta, the core will become Active, and can be used in the making of &6Infinity&r."
				""
				"Be very careful with your cores! Putting any core into the wrong color Crucible will destroy the Core so violently, that only the liquid embodiment of nothingness, &6Null&r, remains."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"To save you a bit of time looking through some of the many Crucible recipes in &bEMI&r, we have created the following diagrams."
				""
				"[\"\",{\"text\":\"All of these images are available in higher resolution in \"},{\"underlined\":true,\"text\":\"Monifactory's Discord Server.\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"70026930847E8EC0\"}}]"
				""
				"&lThe 12 Prismatic Core recipes - Normal Mode&r (Chromatic Transcendence)"
				"{image:monifactory:textures/quests/prismac_priscore.png width:200 height:200 align:center}"
				""
				"Note that a prismatic core of color Magenta refers to an Active Prismatic Core, and White refers to Supercritical."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&lChromatic Stabilizers and Capacitors&r (Chromatic Transcendence)"
				"{image:monifactory:textures/quests/prismac_stabs_caps.png width:200 height:200 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&lThe 12 Prismatic Core recipes - Hard/Expert Mode&r (Chromatic Transcendence)"
